      </version>
      <version name="2.1.0" author="Justin Johnson" time="2026-10-31T16:22:57Z">
        <changelog><![CDATA[Themes, a theme editor and clearer text
- Every colour and opacity in ReEQ2 can now be themed, and 16 themes come with it: Default, High Contrast, Synthwave, Paper, Amber, Ocean, Forest, Mono, Midnight Neon, Sunset, Glacier, Matcha, Rosé, Phosphor, Fjord and Espresso
- The ReEQ2 Theme Editor action (search the Actions window for "ReEQ2 Theme Editor") edits them on a preview of ReEQ2: click anything to pick its colour, then use the colour picker, whole-theme hue, saturation and brightness, band colour harmonies and a gallery of themes; open ReEQ2 windows follow your changes as you make them
- The editor can also set the size new ReEQ2 windows open at; an update puts it back to 922 x 564, and the editor offers to apply your size again
- Settings shows the theme in use
- Text uses one consistent set of sizes, the smallest text is larger, and secondary text and the grid lines are a little brighter
- A small speed-up in the listen filter (thanks, Tale)]]></changelog>
