      <version name="2.2.0" author="Justin Johnson" time="2026-11-05T12:17:35Z">
        <changelog><![CDATA[Closer analogue high end, a UI size setting and larger text
- The filters match their analogue curves more closely near Nyquist, including bands set above it. Projects keep their band settings and automation, but high-frequency bands can sound a little different
- UI size, 100% to 200%, under Settings > Display, for displays where the text is small (such as 1080p at 100% scaling): it scales the whole window, as far as the window size allows. Each ReEQ2 saves its own size with the project, or follows the default
- The ReEQ2 Theme Editor sets the default UI size (125% until you change it), and open ReEQ2 windows follow it
- Larger frequency and dB labels, dB range button, and filter names in the Shape and Stereo pickers
- Settings is laid out in two columns
- Double-click a dial, dynamics knob or toolbar field to reset it to its default; Alt+double-click (Option on macOS) opens the value stepper
- The Theme Editor's own text is larger]]></changelog>
